<title>USA: Eurogas option held by Bishop's Trust.</title>
<headline>Eurogas option held by Bishop's Trust.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurogas Inc said the Trustees of Bernice Pauahi Bishop recently acquired an option to buy 2 million of the company's restricted common shares.</p>
<p>Eurogas declined to disclosed the terms for acquiring the option, which entitles Bishop's Trust to buy stock for $3.50 per share if exercised prior to 90 days after the company's Polish subsidiary reaches an agreement with Texaco Inc to develop Eurogas' coal bed methane concession.</p>
<p>Thereafter, the company said, the trust will have the right to purchase the shares at $4.50 each until December 31, 1997; and, thereafter, at $6.00 per share until December 31, 1998, when the option will expire.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
